  "findings": [
    "The training set contains 590,540 transactions: 20,663 fraudulent (3.50%) and 569,877 legitimate (96.50%). This is a strongly imbalanced target distribution.",
    "TransactionAmt is right-skewed: the overall median is 68.77, the mean is 135.03, and the 99th percentile is 1104.00. The plot uses a log10 amount axis so the long tail and dense low-value region are both visible.",
    "Fraudulent transaction amount median is 75.00 versus 68.50 for legitimate transactions. This is a descriptive difference and does not establish a cause.",
    "ProductCD category C has the highest observed fraud rate (11.69%, n=68,519); the largest category by volume is W (n=439,670). Rates are accompanied by Wilson 95% intervals and should be read with category sizes.",
    "Average missingness is 84.5% across the 40 identity columns and 41.3% across the 392 transaction feature columns in the merged training table. Missingness includes transactions without a linked identity record.",
    "Identity attributes are present for 11,318/20,663 fraudulent transactions (54.77%) and 132,915/569,877 legitimate transactions (23.32%), where presence means at least one joined identity field is nonmissing. This difference is descriptive only.",
    "Among card4 categories with at least 1,000 transactions, discover has the highest observed fraud rate (7.73%, n=6,651).",
    "Among card6 categories with at least 1,000 transactions, credit has the highest observed fraud rate (6.68%, n=148,986)."
  ],
